@startuml usecase
title FinRisk - Investor use cases

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial
skinparam ActorBorderColor #3b6ea5
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #e8f1fa
skinparam UsecaseBorderColor #3b6ea5
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor #f6f9fc
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #fff9d6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #c2b96a

actor "Investor" as inv

rectangle "FinRisk API" {
  usecase "Register and manage own user" as UC1
  usecase "Create or list own accounts" as UC2
  usecase "Browse available assets"      as UC3
  usecase "Buy an asset"                 as UC4
  usecase "Sell an asset"                as UC5
  usecase "View portfolio holdings and value" as UC6
  usecase "View risk score and breakdown"     as UC7
  usecase "View transaction history"     as UC8
}

inv --> UC1
inv --> UC2
inv --> UC3
inv --> UC4
inv --> UC5
inv --> UC6
inv --> UC7
inv --> UC8

note as N1
  **What this shows.**
  The Investor (the only actor today) can trigger any of the
  8 use cases (ovals) exposed by the FinRisk API.
  Each line means "the investor can use that feature".
  Use cases map roughly 1:1 to endpoint groups in
  openapi.yaml. No admin or analyst role exists.
end note

@enduml
